{{also|vollur|vøllur|vǫllr|Völlur}}

==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|vǫllr|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Germanic|walþuz|lang=is}}. Cognate with Faroese {{term|vøllur|lang=fo}}, Norwegian {{term|voll|lang=no}}, Old English {{term|weald}} (English {{term|weald|lang=en}}, {{term|wold|lang=en}}) and Old High German {{term|wald|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Wald}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvœtlʏr/|lang=is}} ({{audio|is-völlur.ogg|listen}})
*: {{rhymes|œtlʏr|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|vallar|vellir}}

# [[field]], [[lawn]]
# [[airfield]], [[airport]]
#: ''Ertu kominn út á '''völl'''?''
#:: Have you arrived at the '''airport'''?
#: ''Ég [[fara út á völl|fór út á '''völl''']] til að sækja vin minn frá Frakklandi.''
#:: I went to the '''airport''' to pick up my friend from France.
# [[field]], [[playing field]]

